<</Author(The Alberta Disability System Breakdown)/Creator(ReportLab Platypus + pikepdf \(ADSB build chain\))/Producer(pikepdf 10.5.1)/Subject(A long-form documentation piece tracing a single operating principle across six distinct historical and contemporary expressions: the Sexual Sterilization Act period \(1928-1972\), the structural-eugenic framework persisting after repeal, the mandatory AISH-to-ADAP transition under Bill 12 \(2025\), the information asymmetry condition, the institutional rebuild under the Compassionate Intervention Act, and the documented cross-Canada expansion of that institutional rebuild across Alberta, Saskatchewan, British Columbia, Manitoba, Ontario, and New Brunswick. Prepared for submission to the United Nations Special Rapporteur on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.)/Title(Consent Was Never the Point: Alberta's Eugenic Inheritance and Canada's Institutional Rebuild, 1928 \204 Present)>>
endobj

