<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="pikepdf">
 <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
 <rdf:Description rdf:about=""><dc:title xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><rdf:Alt><rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Consent Was Never the Point: Alberta's Eugenic Inheritance and Canada's Institutional Rebuild, 1928 â€” Present</rdf:li></rdf:Alt></dc:title><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><rdf:Seq><rdf:li>The Alberta Disability System Breakdown</rdf:li></rdf:Seq></dc:creator><dc:description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><rdf:Alt><rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">A long-form documentation piece tracing a single operating principle across six distinct historical and contemporary expressions: the Sexual Sterilization Act period (1928-1972), the structural-eugenic framework persisting after repeal, the mandatory AISH-to-ADAP transition under Bill 12 (2025), the information asymmetry condition, the institutional rebuild under the Compassionate Intervention Act, and the documented cross-Canada expansion of that institutional rebuild across Alberta, Saskatchewan, British Columbia, Manitoba, Ontario, and New Brunswick. Prepared for submission to the United Nations Special Rapporteur on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.</rdf:li></rdf:Alt></dc:description><dc:subject xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><rdf:Seq><rdf:li>Disability policy</rdf:li><rdf:li>Eugenics</rdf:li><rdf:li>Canada disability legislation</rdf:li><rdf:li>Alberta legislation</rdf:li><rdf:li>AISH</rdf:li><rdf:li>ADAP</rdf:li><rdf:li>Bill 12</rdf:li><rdf:li>Compassionate Intervention Act</rdf:li><rdf:li>Cross-Canada institutional rebuild</rdf:li><rdf:li>CRPD</rdf:li><rdf:li>UN Special Rapporteur</rdf:li><rdf:li>Public advocacy</rdf:li></rdf:Seq></dc:subject><dc:publisher xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">The Alberta Disability System Breakdown</dc:publisher><dc:rights xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><rdf:Alt><rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Free to share, print, and post under attribution to The Alberta Disability System Breakdown. No individual byline is asserted. The campaign holds the work as collective record.</rdf:li></rdf:Alt></dc:rights><dc:identifier xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">albertadisabilitysystembreakdown.netlify.app</dc:identifier><dc:date xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">2026-05-23</dc:date><xmp:CreatorTool xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/">ReportLab Platypus + pikepdf (ADSB build chain)</xmp:CreatorTool><xmp:MetadataDate xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/">2026-05-24T04:37:17.461817+00:00</xmp:MetadataDate><pdf:Producer xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/">pikepdf 10.5.1</pdf:Producer></rdf:Description></rdf:RDF>
